        "metadata": {
          "category": "stories",
          "media": {
            "duration": 4769,
            "fileSize": 77342183
          },
          "author": "Andy Stanton",
          "description": "Shabba me whiskers! It’s the fourth fantastic Mr Gum story, read by the author and with music and sound effects. A fantastic book for boys and girls aged 7-10 years old. \n\nGood evening, children, on this dark and windy night. Now, come gather round the fireplace, for ‘tis time for strange tales to be spun.\n\nLike the tale of Polly and that old tumbledown windmill by the riverside. But just what is the windmill’s terrible secret? Why is Mr Gum lurk-lurk-lurkin’ about? And how much does Old Granny know?\n\nGather closer, children, for all shall be revealed… BRRR! SPOOKY!",
          "audioPreviewUrl": "https://audio-previews-media.api.yotoplay.com/audio-previews/6cf89344938084f1b92219093d02902dd188ec2aaf672f74a5a482d7c8844d80/cPp3wIbYYAWz5lf0VIbh1gCZ3LR47VzNDSb60ge-EU8.mp3",
